&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Miles per gallon&quot;,&quot;scale&quot;:{&quot;zero&quot;:false}}}}]}\"><div data-phiz-view wire:ignore></div></div>\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega@6.4.0/build/vega.min.js\" integrity=\"sha384-VKdcJr3ZaBIJMbVcopTAI/JEuUkSY6qnwVu9iLuw0DnQ9gQ1JjsfZJhXFQAgNi43\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-lite@6.4.3/build/vega-lite.min.js\" integrity=\"sha384-9/70gNCfOu6G7xXvkdreMfuqAEsoaGJVXV2BN/JLRXkSmcGvnMqtsRx8HZtUWAvI\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-embed@7.3.0/build/vega-embed.min.js\" integrity=\"sha384-Muy1QRxYFeNrA1zShc1KtN4OfipkR/61gt+HWqN57c1Zxu3Oe16TsilsruVVjfKL\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n<script>/*\n * phiz: renders [data-phiz] elements with vega-embed, and re-renders when their spec changes (Livewire morphs).\n * A [data-phiz-deferred] element fetches its spec from its [data-phiz-spec] link when it nears the viewport, then\n * renders like any other.\n */\n(function () {\n  if (window.Phiz) return;\n  var views = new WeakMap();\n  var dark = window.matchMedia ? window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)') : null;\n\n  function parse(json, fallback) {\n    if (!json) return fallback;\n    try { return JSON.parse(json); } catch (e) { console.error('phiz: invalid JSON', e); return fallback; }\n  }\n\n  function target(el) {\n    var view = el.querySelector(':scope > [data-phiz-view]');\n    if (!view) {\n      view = document.createElement('div');\n      view.setAttribute('data-phiz-view', '');\n      view.setAttribute('wire:ignore', '');\n      el.appendChild(view);\n    }\n    return view;\n  }\n\n  function render(el) {\n    var embed = Phiz.embed || window.vegaEmbed;\n    if (!embed) { pending = true; return; }\n    var json = el.getAttribute('data-phiz');\n    var optionsJson = el.getAttribute('data-phiz-options') || '';\n    var key = json + '\\u0000' + optionsJson + '\\u0000' + (dark && dark.matches ? 'dark' : 'light');\n    var state = views.get(el);\n    if (state && state.key === key) return;\n    var spec = parse(json, null);\n    if (!spec) return;\n    var options = parse(optionsJson, {});\n    if (options.theme === 'auto') {\n      if (dark && dark.matches) options.theme = 'dark'; else delete options.theme;\n    }\n    if (state && state.view) state.view.finalize();\n    // Each render draws into its own element, so a slow, superseded render cannot replace a newer chart.\n    var token = {};\n    var holder = document.createElement('div');\n    target(el).appendChild(holder);\n    views.set(el, { key: key, token: token, view: null });\n    Promise.resolve(embed(holder, spec, options)).then(function (result) {\n      var current = views.get(el);\n      if (!current || current.token !== token) { result.view.finalize(); holder.remove(); return; }\n      Array.prototype.slice.call(holder.parentNode.children).forEach(function (child) { if (child !== holder) child.remove(); });\n      current.view = result.view;\n      el.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('phiz:rendered', { detail: { view: result.view }, bubbles: true }));\n    }).catch(function (error) {\n      var current = views.get(el);\n      if (!current || current.token !== token) { holder.remove(); return; }\n      console.error('phiz:', error);\n      holder.textContent = 'Chart error: ' + error.message;\n    });\n  }\n\n  function load(el) {\n    if (el.hasAttribute('data-phiz') || el.getAttribute('data-phiz-deferred') === 'loading') return;\n    var link = el.querySelector('a[data-phiz-spec]');\n    if (!link) return;\n    el.setAttribute('data-phiz-deferred', 'loading');\n    fetch(link.href).then(function (response) {\n      if (!response.ok) throw new Error(response.status + ' ' + response.statusText);\n      return response.text();\n    }).then(function (json) {\n      el.setAttribute('data-phiz-deferred', 'loaded');\n      el.setAttribute('data-phiz', json);\n    }).catch(function (error) {\n      el.setAttribute('data-phiz-deferred', 'failed');\n      console.error('phiz: cannot load ' + link.href, error);\n    });\n  }\n\n  var nearby = window.IntersectionObserver ? new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {\n    entries.forEach(function (entry) {\n      if (entry.isIntersecting) { nearby.unobserve(entry.target); load(entry.target); }\n    });\n  }, { rootMargin: '200px' }) : null;\n\n  function defer(el) {\n    if (el.hasAttribute('data-phiz') || el.getAttribute('data-phiz-deferred')) return;\n    if (nearby) nearby.observe(el); else load(el);\n  }\n\n  function scan(root) {\n    if (root.nodeType !== 1) return;\n    if (root.hasAttribute('data-phiz')) render(root);\n    root.querySelectorAll('[data-phiz]').forEach(render);\n    if (root.hasAttribute('data-phiz-deferred')) defer(root);\n    root.querySelectorAll('[data-phiz-deferred]').forEach(defer);\n  }\n\n  function release(root) {\n    if (root.nodeType !== 1) return;\n    var nodes = root.hasAttribute('data-phiz') ? [root] : [];\n    root.querySelectorAll('[data-phiz]').forEach(function (n) { nodes.push(n); });\n    nodes.forEach(function (n) {\n      if (n.isConnected) return;\n      var state = views.get(n);\n      if (state && state.view) state.view.finalize();\n      views.delete(n);\n    });\n  }\n\n  var pending = false;\n  var Phiz = window.Phiz = {\n    embed: null,\n    render: render,\n    scan: function () { scan(document.documentElement); },\n    view: function (el) { var s = views.get(el); return s ? s.view : null; }\n  };\n\n  new MutationObserver(function (mutations) {\n    mutations.forEach(function (m) {\n      if (m.type === 'attributes') { render(m.target); return; }\n      m.addedNodes.forEach(scan);\n      m.removedNodes.forEach(release);\n    });\n  }).observe(document.documentElement, { subtree: true, childList: true, attributes: true, attributeFilter: ['data-phiz', 'data-phiz-options'] });\n\n  if (dark && dark.addEventListener) dark.addEventListener('change', function () { Phiz.scan(); });\n\n  function start() { pending = false; Phiz.scan(); }\n  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', start); else start();\n  window.addEventListener('load', function () { if (pending) start(); });\n})();</script>\n```\n\nFuel economy against weight, with a least-squares line.\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Features {#what-the-kernel-provides}\n\n- State across cells, including `use` imports and declared functions and\n  classes.\n- Tracebacks that name the cell and the line, instead of `eval()'d code`.\n- HTML tables for phibble data frames and charts for phiz plots, plus\n  `toHtml()` and `toMimeBundle()` hooks for any other class.\n- `Juphyter\\display()`, which shows a value part way through a cell.\n- Completion of variables, functions, classes, and members.\n- Interrupting a running cell with the stop button, when PHP has the `pcntl`\n  extension.\n- Loading the nearest `vendor/autoload.php` above the notebook, so a notebook\n  inside a Composer project can use that project's classes and packages.\n\njuphyter requires none of the PHPstats packages. It runs plain PHP, and it\nformats a phibble data frame or a phiz plot when those packages are\ninstalled.\n\n## Architecture {#how-it-works}\n\nA Python program built on [ipykernel](https://github.com/ipython/ipykernel)\nhandles the Jupyter protocol, and a PHP process runs the cells. They talk over\na Unix socket. That is why an install needs Python as well as PHP, and why the\nkernel runs on macOS and Linux only.\n\n## Documentation\n\n- [Installation](install.qmd): requirements, install commands, and the\n  installation check.\n- [First steps](get-started.qmd): cells, state, imports, errors, and rich\n  output.\n- [Reference](reference.qmd): commands, the display API, and configuration.\n\n",
